$DIR/test.p:2:46: volatile element type T must be an integer, bool or pointer
    volatile[T] makes every read and write of T exactly one load or store. That
    is only possible for a value the processor moves in one instruction: an
    integer, a bool, a pointer, or a packed type backed by an integer.
    (see "volatile[T]" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.15)
    (run "pluto explain E2108" for a longer explanation)
